WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
A skull lies half buried in the ground.

2
00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:05.980
The animal it belonged to is long gone.

3
00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:11.110
Its muscles, its gut, its last
meal: none of them is left.

4
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.020
But the teeth remain,
set in the jaw: incisors,

5
00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.170
canines, premolars and molars.

6
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.570
Nobody can watch this animal eat.

7
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.980
So how can its teeth reveal what it ate?

8
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.650
In this mission, you'll read
a skull like an investigator:

9
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:33.170
each tooth, then the jaw, the jaw joint
and the places where muscles attached.

10
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.670
Then you'll compare it with living
mammals whose diets we know,

11
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.280
and state what you can deduce,
and from which evidence.

12
00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:45.240
Your mission: find out how a skull's
teeth can reveal what its owner ate.
